  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans and documents: Site Location Plan; Drawing number&nbsp;2973/EP1 [Existing and Proposed Ground Floor Layout]; Site and Street Photos; Covering Letter and Design and Access Statement (ref.&nbsp;AW/HL/SIL002-25-0/7317) prepared by Woodswhur, dated 15th April 2025.&nbsp;",
    "The development hereby permitted shall be begun before the expiration of three years from the date of this permission.",
    "The use hereby permitted shall not be open to customers outside the following times:&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;09.00 to 00.00 hours, Monday to\r\nSunday.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;CM5&quot; style=&quot;margin-bottom:0cm;text-align:justify&quot;&gt;&lt;span lang=&quot;EN-US&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "The sui generis use hereby permitted shall only be used for the purposes specified in the application.",
    "The change of use hereby permitted shall not be occupied or open to members of the\r\npublic until evidence of Secured by Design (SBD) certification is submitted to\r\nthe Local Planning Authority in writing. Otherwise, written justification should be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority as to why such certification cannot be achieved, including a scheme of the proposed SBD measures that can be reasonably achieved.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;Secure by design measures shall be\r\nimplemented on site and the development shall be retained in accordance\r\nwith the approved details.&amp;nbsp;",
    "The use hereby permitted shall not be occupied or open to members of the public until a management strategy including administrative measures to address and deter anti-social behaviour;&amp;nbsp;general waste management measures; and measures for managing noise from the development; has been submitted to and approved in writing by the local planning authority.&amp;nbsp; The operation of the premises shall be in strict accordance with the agreed management strategy unless otherwise agreed in writing by the local planning authority."
